<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amplats says only small mines hit by strike.</title>
<headline>Amplats says only small mines hit by strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Anglo American Platinum Corp Ltd said on Monday that its main Rustenburg Platinum Holdings Ltd unit was working normally on Monday despite a one-day general strike call.  </p>
<p>However, production at the smaller mines of Lebowa Platinum Mines Ltd and Potgietersrust Platinums Ltd had been halted by the action.  </p>
<p>&quot;Our main mines at Rustenburg are not affected and that's where 90 percent of our employees are. But the two mines in the Northern Province, Lebowa and PP Rust, have seen action,&quot; said spokesman Johan Adler.</p>
<p>There was no morning shift at Lebowa while at PP Rust workers arrived for work but then went on a stoppage.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
